-- title:
--   Exact q=5 outer counts and unchanged fourth-level parent Z profiles
-- statement:
--   This fixes the integer data for the existing $q=5$ fourth-power DWZ candidate, without changing its public coarse distribution or its parent Z profiles.
--
--   The 45 labels are in the order of the public address table $\sigma(c)=(I_c,J_c,L_c)$, with $I_c+J_c+L_c=8$. The outer scale is $A=2\cdot10^{15}$; the stored natural numbers $a_c$ are the corresponding candidate numerators. Separate tables store the X/Y and Z marginal numerators.
--
--   For each label $c$, the definition records the unchanged rational-replay parent Z profile as a positive denominator $d_c$ and five counts $b_{c,0},\ldots,b_{c,4}$, together with its actual integer prescribed-Z profile object:
--   $$
--   p_c(\ell)=\frac{b_{c,\ell}}{d_c},
--   \qquad \sum_{\ell=0}^{4}b_{c,\ell}=d_c.
--   $$
--   Here $\ell$ is the left-square grade of a fourth-power Z coordinate. Constructor proofs establish only positivity of $d_c$ and normalization of the five counts. No coupled-child canonicalization, averaging, endpoint substitution, or parent-profile retuning is performed.
--
--   The data are extracted from the existing exact rational replay of the released numerical certificate, not asserted to be the literal binary64 numbers in the MAT file. Positivity and normalization of the outer distribution, its equality to the public rational $\alpha$, the supported-address bijection, exact marginal identities, and split-support conditions are separate proof obligations. These definitions contain no entropy estimate, tensor extraction assumption, or matrix-multiplication exponent claim.
-- source:
--   Duan, Wu, and Zhou, Faster Matrix Multiplication via Asymmetric Hashing, arXiv:2210.10173v5, Definitions 3.5 and 3.7 and Sections 6.1–6.2; released fourth-power q=5 numerical data power4_dup_2.371919.mat, https://osf.io/dta6p/files/zx3yf . Outer coarseAddress and alpha are the existing public rational-global data (f99d9be9-2a29-4f1d-a088-6deb77a2e185). The 45 unchanged parent profiles are entries object139–object183 of the existing exact rational-replay tensor ledger, whose extraction rounds source entries at denominator10^15 and normalizes exactly. This data definition does not import or rely on the ledger's scalar-induction facade.

